<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Labashi-Marduk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 556 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Labashi-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marduk">Marduk</a> was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> for a few months in 556 BCE, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neriglissar">Neriglissar</a> while still young. He was murdered in a conspiracy of court officials, which brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabonidus">Nabonidus</a> to the throne. His brief reign was the last of four in six years after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a>, showing the instability of the Neo-Babylonian monarchy.</p></div>
